message.content:
Design an implementation plan for adding the ability in Vinyl Angel's Gameplay Tab (`VinylPlayer.tsx`) to add the playlist whose song is playing to an existing custom playlist.

Context and background:
- Application path: `D:\My Drive\SandBox Projetcs\universe-25\src\apps\vinyl-angel`
- In `VinylPlayer.tsx`, when a song is playing, `currentTrack` holds the track metadata, where `currentTrack.channel` is the origin playlist / channel of the song.
- Custom playlists are defined in `types.ts` as:
  ```ts
  export interface CustomPlaylist {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    emoji: string;
    description?: string;
    channels: string[];
    compatible_timeblocks?: string[];
    created_at: string;
    updated_at: string;
  }
  ```
- Custom playlists are persisted in SQLite `playlists.db` via `saveCustomPlaylist(projectId, playlist)` in `services/engine.ts`.
- In `useVinylStore.ts`, `customPlaylists` is kept in Zustand store, updated via `updateCustomPlaylist(playlist)` and `addCustomPlaylist(playlist)`.
- In `VinylPlayer.tsx`, `currentTrack.channel` is currently displayed in the track metadata line (lines 2247-2270) right below the track title.
- Also in `VinylPlayer.tsx`, `PlaylistManagerModal` or a dedicated dropdown / popover can be used.

Requirements for the plan:
1. Exact UI design and interaction in `VinylPlayer.tsx` for adding the currently playing song's channel/playlist to an existing custom playlist.
2. Handling states: whether the channel is already in the playlist, adding it, updating the store, persisting to backend `playlists.db`, and providing toast feedback.
3. Option to create a new custom playlist with this channel pre-selected (reusing `PlaylistManagerModal` or inline quick creation).
4. Edge cases: no track playing, no custom playlists exist yet, channel already added to all playlists, error handling.
5. Provide a detailed, step-by-step implementation plan.

